  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "📝 About Ward 5",
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Ward No. 5 of Kathmandu Metropolitan City covers Hadigaun, Bhatbhateni, Bishalnagar and surrounding neighborhoods. Rooted in Kirat–Licchavi history, it is known for its rich Newar heritage, ancient temples, traditional hitis, falchas and the unique Kahi Nabhako Jatra. With approximately 18,000+ residents, the ward blends historic identity with modern urban life."
    },
    {
      "title": "🏛️ Cultural Significance",
      "type": "list",
      "content": [
        "One of Kathmandu Valley’s oldest settlements, with Kirat–Licchavi heritage",
        "Home to the historic Kailashkut Bhawan palace complex",
        "Known for the unique Kahi Nabhako Jatra (wheel-less chariot festival)",
        "Rich in traditional hitis, inars, falchas and public taps",
        "Home to 95+ heritage monuments recognized by the Department of Archaeology",
        "A vibrant Newar cultural and traditional residential community"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "🗂️ Data Source",
      "type": "list",
      "content": [
        "Administrative Boundary: Digitized from ward-level administrative records",
        "Jatra Routes: Ward Office",
        "Hiti, Inar, Falcha, Public Taps & Temples: Ward Office",
        "Educational Areas, Landmarks & Road Network: OpenStreetMap (OSM)"
      ]
    },
    {
